From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:34:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: switch the IWLAN transport on for Wi-Fi calling

The modem takes the Wi-Fi calling configuration and then does nothing with it: the IMS log shows
wifi_call: 2 and wfc_preference stored and acknowledged, and no ePDG registration is ever
attempted, so isVowifiEnabled stays false and a forced WFC call reports "connect to a wireless
network" while connected to one.

persist.data.iwlan.enable is the QTI switch for the IWLAN data path an ePDG tunnel rides on; both
netmgrd and qmuxd read it. Stock sets it on this device and this port did not carry it over.

Worth recording: the T-Mobile config in the modem image does carry ePDG --
mcfg_sw/generic/na/tmo/commerci/mcfg_sw.mbn has epdg_fqdn ss.epdg.epc.mnc260.mcc310 and IWLAN in
its Supported_RAT_Priority_List -- so the capability is present and this is worth pursuing.
---
 device.mk | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index d2d6d0f..b38fb03 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -391,6 +391,18 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += libshim_vtsurface
 # want to avoid blocking the binder thread".
 PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += ro.telephony.block_binder_thread_on_incoming_calls=false
 
+# persist.data.iwlan.enable is the QTI switch for the IWLAN data path, which is what an ePDG tunnel
+# rides on. Stock sets it on this device and this port did not carry it over. Without it the modem
+# accepts the Wi-Fi calling configuration -- the log shows wifi_call: 2 and wfc_preference stored
+# and acknowledged -- and then never attempts to register, because the transport it would use is
+# switched off. netmgrd and qmuxd both read it.
+#
+# Not copied from stock's build.prop, despite being next to it there:
+#   persist.radio.app_hw_mbn_path -- nothing in this image reads it, and stock's value points at
+#     /firmware/image/modem_pr/..., which does not exist; the real tree is /firmware/image/mdm/....
+#   persist.radio.VT_CAM_INTERFACE -- video telephony is deliberately off (config_device_vt_available).
+PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += persist.data.iwlan.enable=true
+
 # nanopb 0.2.8, for libril-qc-qmi-1.so alone. See nanopb-0.2.8/Android.bp for why a second copy of
 # nanopb has to exist at all.
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += libnanopb_legacy
